  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Lav has an array AAA of size NNN. He noticed that Chef is initially standing at the **first** index of the array.\n\nWhile standing at the ithi^{th}ith index (1≤i&lt;N)(1 \\leq i \\lt N)(1≤i&lt;N) of the array, Chef can perform the following types of jumps:\n\n\nJump&nbsp;1\\texttt{Jump 1}Jump&nbsp;1: Jump to the immediate next index jjj such that AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​ have the **same** parity.\nJump&nbsp;2\\texttt{Jump 2}Jump&nbsp;2: Jump to the immediate next index jjj such that AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​ have **different** parity.\nGiven that Chef can perform Jump&nbsp;2\\texttt{Jump 2}Jump&nbsp;2 **at most once**, Lav wants to find the **minimum** number of jumps required by the Chef to reach the **last** index of the array.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_{1},A_2, \\ldots, A_{N}A1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **minimum** number of jumps required by the Chef to reach the **last** index of the array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1042 \\leq N \\leq 10^42≤N≤104",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_{i} \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n1 2 3 4\n4\n2 1 3 4",
        "output": "2\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111:  The minimum number of jumps required by the Chef to reach the last index is 222.\nChef is initially standing at index 111.\n\nChef chooses Jump 2\\texttt{Jump 2}Jump 2 and jumps to index 222 as it is the immediate next element with different parity.\nChef chooses Jump 1\\texttt{Jump 1}Jump 1 and jumps to index 444 as it is the immediate next element with the same parity.\n\nTest Case 222:  The minimum number of jumps required by the Chef to reach the last index is 111.\nChef is currently standing at index 111.\n\nChef chooses Jump 1\\texttt{Jump 1}Jump 1 and jumps to index 444 as it is the immediate next element with the same parity."
      }
    ]
  },
